;; A query's `:expect` lists its projection classes — the goal's atoms under
;; its rows (docs/ein/user/03-syntax-and-semantics/12-query.md) — so a listed fact the
;; goal does not match is not a class of it. A claim about the state, which
;; `(q A H1)` here would be, is the region claim's, `(solve … :expect (region
;; …))`. The loader refuses the listing, naming the fact and the claim that
;; would state it.

(relation p Thing Place :why "p holds of {?3} and {?4}")
(relation q Thing Place :why "q holds of {?3} and {?4}")
(p A H1)
(q A H1)
(query :goal (p A ?h) :expect (model (q A H1)))
